> Module Ofek_hadash_cases

> Using Ofek_hadash

# Ofek Hadash — the worked cases, run against the emitted Catala module

These are the same three teachers as `ofek-cases.l4`, asking the same
questions and expecting the same figures. They are written **by hand**, and
that is the point of the file: `l4 catala` is supposed to lower each `#ASSERT`
directive into a Catala `#[test]` scope, and on this module it does not —
it reports each one as "did not become a Catala `#[test]` scope … that is a
lowering bug, please report it", and emits the disclosure instead of the test.

So without this file the emitted module is typechecked but never *run*, and a
lowering that quietly produced different arithmetic would pass unnoticed. With
it, the numbers below are computed by `catala interpret` from the emitted
module alone — no L4 involved — and compared against the figures the L4
encoding asserts. See NOTES.md § 7 for the minimal reproduction of the lowering
bug and for what was measured.

Regenerating `ofek_hadash.catala_en` does not regenerate this file. If the
encoding changes, these expectations must be updated by hand — which is the
cost of the bug, and the reason it is worth reporting rather than working
around silently.

```catala
declaration scope YaelInSeptember2024:
  output pay content decimal

scope YaelInSeptember2024:
  definition pay equals
    (output of Ofek_hadash.TheMonthlyPayOf with {
       -- the_teacher: Ofek_hadash.ATeacher {
            -- qualification: AcademicHoldsARecognisedFirstDegree
            -- seniority_in_years: 11.0
            -- rank: 4.0
            -- stage_of_education: AJuniorHighSchool
            -- fraction_of_a_full_post: 1.0
            -- first_role: Present content
                 HomeroomTeacherOfAClassOtherThanTheFirstGrade
            -- second_role: Absent
            -- classes_in_the_coordinated_grade_level: 0.0
            -- units_of_the_school_role_supplement: 0.0
          }
       -- the_date: |2024-09-01|
       -- the_value_of_any_seniority_step_taken_in_september_2025: 0.0
     }).the_monthly_pay_of

